}
```

## Why This Rule Exists

1. **Prevents Errors**: Adding code later without braces can cause logic errors
2. **Improves Readability**: Clear visual separation of control flow and method boundaries
3. **Consistency**: Uniform code style across the project and all languages
4. **Maintainability**: Easier to modify and debug code
5. **Prevents Git Diffs**: Adding braces later creates unnecessary diff noise
6. **Cross-Language Consistency**: Same formatting rules apply regardless of programming language
7. **Method Clarity**: Braces on new lines make method boundaries more obvious

